Subject: Exclude the enterprise wl tree from the server build

Description: Downgrade a licensed mode to unlicensed at the three feature helpers and stop the server from compiling packages under wl.
Origin: DHI-internal (license exclusion)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate 8b9cac335313bd403c0d33e299d07b4283816a07
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/semitechnologies-weaviate/tests -count=1 -run TestMeta -timeout 20m` expect "PASS"
Forwarded: not-needed (community package must build without the enterprise tree)
Drop-When: never: the wl license grants no right to redistribute that tree

The enterprise tree under wl is not covered by the BSD license that applies outside that directory. A key follows the unlicensed path those helpers already test, including the startup warning and the stale wipe-marker cleanup. Licensed callbacks remain only so this build does not import wl, and they panic if a mode helper stops downgrading.

